The bundled Excalidraw engine and its dependencies retain their original notices.
Full, version-labelled dependency notices ship in dist/adapters/excalidraw/engine/licenses/.
The shipped bundle-sbom.json binds actual output bytes and lock-resolved package instances
to full notices. LICENSES.json also records SHA-bound upstream embedded components,
including Excalidraw's fonteditor-core and harfbuzzjs WASM notices and pica's Browserify
dependencies. Embedded entry-source matches establish attribution; they do not reconstruct
the historical dependency resolution or certify all compiled subroutines. The bounded
source/banner/map sweep and its limits are recorded explicitly. npm audit only covers
lock-resolved installed instances and cannot clear components inside upstream prebundles.
Reviewed deviations in the emitted engine are recorded in its SBOM. Installed upstream
files and full license bodies remain unchanged.
Font license texts and source/hash metadata ship with the engine; source metadata is
src/adapters/excalidraw/assets/LICENSES.json. Cascadia and Assistant use SIL OFL 1.1.
